'''Juryrigg'''{{Refn|End credits for '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''' and '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]'''|group = credits}} is the [[Omnitrix]]'s DNA sample of a [[Planchaküle]] from the planet [[Aul-Turrhen]].{{Refn|''[[Ben 10 Ultimate Alien: The Ultimate Ending]]''; [[:File:Dagon DVD 1.PNG|file]]|group = DVD}}

==Appearance==
Juryrigg is a small [[Wikipedia:Gremlin|Gremlin]]-like alien with four-fingered hands, three-toed feet, and a devil-like tail. He is small in stature, only about as big as a [[Human (Classic)|human]] head.

In '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''', Juryrigg had reddish-orange skin and wore the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]] symbol on his chest.

In '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''', Juryrigg's skin is much smoother and recolored crimson-red. He now wears an aviator's outfit which comes with an ascot. His eyes now have black pupils, his ears are now spiked, his sharp teeth jut out of his mouth, and his nose is bigger. He also has a spike on his chin and one near each of his eyes. The [[Omnitrix (Omniverse)|Omnitrix]] symbol is now on his waist.

<gallery hideaddbutton="true" bordercolor="transparent" captionalign="center" spacing="small">
Juryrigg with Goggles.png|Juryrigg wearing his goggles in ''[[Return to Forever]]''
</gallery>

==Personality==
Juryrigg has a strong desire to break and remake machines, making him difficult to control.

Juryrigg has a mischievous (and twisted) sense of humor, as seen when he turned [[Will Harangue]] into an alien as punishment for all the smear campaigns and crimes he committed against [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] and other aliens.<ref name="RtF">''[[Return to Forever]]''</ref>

Juryrigg has several catchphrases, such as "Juryrigg disassemble!", "FIX FIX FIX FIX FIX!", and "Reassemble, disassemble!"

==Powers and Abilities==
<gallery type="slideshow">
RtF (527).png|Enhanced Intelligence/Technological Expertise
FAtC (346).png|Technological Disassembly
TEC (392).png|Technological Repairment
Juryrigg Technological Modification.png|Technological Modification
RoE (319).png|Technology Creation
RoE (317).png|Enhanced Strength
MI (142).png|Enhanced Durability
GF (353).png|Enhanced Agility
</gallery>
{{Quote|"Ben, listen to me. Whatever Juryrigg broke, he can fix."<br>"He can? How do you know?"<br>"Breaking things couldn't be his only power. It just couldn't."|[[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] and [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]].<ref name="TEC">''[[The Eggman Cometh]]''</ref>}}
Juryrigg boasts an impressive intellect,{{Refn|[[:File:2020-06-14 Q A With Matt Wayne - Page 18.png]]|group = MW}} describing himself as "smart and stubborn".<ref name="RtF" />

Juryrigg has the ability to completely disassemble any kind of machinery, including [[Rex Salazar (Generator Rex)|Rex Salazar]]'s builds,{{Refn|[[:File:Juryrigg Can Dismantle Rex's Machines.png]]|group = DJW}} in mere seconds. Juryrigg can also construct complex machinery from scratch at a similar rate.<ref name="ROE">''[[Rules of Engagement]]''</ref>

In addition to disassembling machinery, Juryrigg can modify machines after disassembling them.<ref name="MI" /><ref name="GF">''[[Gone Fishin']]''</ref> Juryrigg is also able to repair technology.<ref name="TEC" /><ref>[[Rook Blonko]]</ref><ref>''[[Let's Do the Time War Again]]''</ref>

Juryrigg can dismantle and rebuild living mechanical species such as [[Chronosapien|Chronosapiens]].{{Refn|[[:File:Juryrigg Dismantle Living Machines.png]]|group = DJW|name = robots}}

Juryrigg has enhanced strength for his size, being able to break some metal bars that even an [[Appoplexian (Classic)|Appoplexian]] could not break.<ref>''[[Food Around the Corner]]''</ref>

Juryrigg has a degree of enhanced durability, as he was able to withstand being thrown against a destroyed food truck by a [[Rock Monster]].<ref name="MI">''[[Mystery, Incorporeal]]''</ref>

Juryrigg's tail is prehensile.{{Refn|[[:File:Juryrigg Prehensile Tail.png]]|group = DJW}}

===Non-Canon Powers and Abilities===
Juryrigg can instantly teleport to different locations.{{Refn|[[:File:Juryrigg Guidebook Info.png]]|group = guide|name = book}}

Juryrigg can generate smoke bombs for cover.{{Refn|group = guide|name = book}}

==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow">
TEC (107).png|Uncontrollable Habit
MI (141).png|Small Size
</gallery>
Juryrigg has a near uncontrollable habit of breaking and assembling machinery.<ref name="TEC" />

Juryrigg's small size makes him unsuitable for hand-to-hand combat against larger opponents.<ref name="MI" />

== History==
===Ultimate Alien=== 
*Juryrigg first appeared in ''[[The Eggman Cometh]]'', where he began taking apart the brakes in [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]]'s [[Kevin's Car (Original)|car]]. Later, Juryrigg dismantled [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]]'s mutant ray, but soon had to repair and modify it in order to stop the [[Pterodactyl|pterodactyl]] from wreaking havoc on [[Bellwood (Classic)|Bellwood]].
*In ''[[The Ultimate Enemy: Part 1]]'', Juryrigg prepared to battle [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]] and [[Psyphon]] before [[Dagon]] freed himself.
*In ''[[The Ultimate Enemy: Part 2]]'', Juryrigg briefly appeared before reverting.

===Omniverse===
*In ''[[Have I Got a Deal for You]]'', Juryrigg briefly appeared before switching into [[Grey Matter (Classic)|Grey Matter]] as part of an accidental transformation chain.
*In ''[[Gone Fishin']]'', Juryrigg defeated the [[Mechaneer]]s.
*In ''[[Rules of Engagement]]'', Juryrigg fixed up parts of the [[Proto-TRUK]] and created the [[Tenn-Speed]].
*In ''[[Food Around the Corner]]'', Juryrigg tore through a door and fixed the security system.
*In ''[[Return to Forever]]'', Juryrigg disabled the [[Highbreed Pulse Generator]] before it could destroy every alien on [[Earth (Classic)|Earth]], and reprogrammed the machine to instead turn [[Will Harangue]] into an alien.
*In ''[[Mystery, Incorporeal]]'', Juryrigg was defeated by a [[Rock Monster]].
*In ''[[It's a Mad, Mad, Mad Ben World: Part 1]]'', Juryrigg was defeated by [[Mad Ben|Mad]] [[Diamondhead (Classic)|Diamondhead]].
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Juryrigg appeared for a short time when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was cycling through his aliens.

